// THE PROGRAM'S OWN SWITCH (MS-2, the author 2026-10-03: "arguments.missing = false right where a
// satellite word would go"): written once at the top of the file, outside every capsule, it is the
// run's arguments.missing before anything is said about the program or runs in it, and main reads
// it back. tests/arguments_missing_not_written.satl is this file without the line, and answers true.
// check.sh runs both, side by side.

satellite.include(satellite)
arguments.missing = false

satellite.capsule satellite.main(satellite.variable.arguments args)
{
    satellite.console.display(args.missing)
    satellite.return(satellite)
}
